00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.309 align:start position:0%
the european union hosts the group of  seven major  industrial powers in brussels for talks  on the conflict in ukraine  the world economy energy security  climate change  and development the meeting had been  scheduled to take place in sochi russia  in g8 format but the leaders decided in  march to meet without moscow  given its annexation of ukraine's crimea  region  ukraine will top the agenda as the  leaders evaluated a working  dinner the latest developments and what  action might be taken in response to  them  other international issues could also be  raised including syria  libya iran afghanistan north korea  or the middle east during their first  working session  the leaders will turn to the global  economy with talks likely to focus on  trade  and ways to sustain economic growth and  combat unemployment  in light of the ukraine crisis and the  country's role as a transit route for  russian gas  energy security will also be discussed  notably the diversification of routes  and suppliers  clean and low carbon technologies are on  the table too  as the powers seek to cut greenhouse gas  emissions and fight climate change  a final working lunch will be devoted to  development issues  taking stock of previous g7 commitments  and looking at the post 2015 agenda  to complete unfinished parts of the  millennium development goals
 

